    {
      "item_id": "A005-000002-G-002",
      "item_type": "gap",
      "title": "Lifecycle, projection truth, concurrency, and offline states are unconstrained",
      "statement": "The schema requires projection_freshness and projection_health but leaves both as arbitrary strings and defines no failure state, transition legality, revision, sequence, idempotency key, optimistic concurrency token, tombstone, synchronization provenance, pending-upload state, or conflict outcome. Concurrent writers, replay, stale projections, and offline recovery can all yield contradictory records that remain valid; a GUI consuming these fields has no schema-enforced truth vocabulary and may present stale or unhealthy data as current.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "high",
