    {
      "item_id": "A005-000002-G-003",
      "item_type": "gap",
      "title": "Failure, recovery, rollback, and destructive-action semantics are absent",
      "statement": "Despite representing failed attempts, the envelope does not require a failure code, failure phase, retryability, retry count, terminality, partial-output inventory, recovery action, rollback status, compensation reference, quarantine state, or deletion/purge authorization. The optional receipt/detail/content references do not distinguish committed from partial or unsafe outputs, so automation cannot reliably decide whether retry, rollback, preservation, or destructive cleanup is safe.",
